        "diagnosis": "The forward kernel computes prefix sums and subtracts the simplex mass directly from uncentered values. Large offsets erase the subtraction of 1 and the final projection residual in float32. Actual sparse-05 GPU evidence shows 512/512 mismatches: outputs are zero instead of 0.00390625, with inputs unchanged. The passing sparse-01 control has 0/32 mismatches and outputs 0.0625, demonstrating that failure depends on numerical scale and row width. Repair by subtracting the row maximum in float32 before support selection and output calculation. Clamp centered values below -1: these entries cannot have positive simplex mass, and clipping prevents extreme finite inputs from causing overflowing prefix sums. Both transformations preserve the mathematical projection, and neither writes to the input. Compilation and held-out correctness remain unverified because execution feedback is unavailable.",
